<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.6.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01356</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.6.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4028ae2a-f4dc-4729-99a9-77299f73f7d0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>Use the following passage to answer questions 1 – 3.</para>
<para>In a newly formed swamp, it is estimated that there are 500 mosquitoes. The population is estimated to double each
  day.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section><exercise id="_43fa5526-480c-4a1a-b106-126d453a95ff" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Let \(m\) represent the total population of mosquitoes and \(d\) represent the number of days that have
          passed since the first estimate. What is the equation that represents the growth of the mosquito population?
      </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(m=d\cdot 500^2\)</para><para>\(m=2\cdot 500^d\)</para><para>\(m=500\cdot 2^d\)</para><para>\(m=500\cdot d^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.
    </para><para>The correct answer is \(m=500\cdot 2^d\).
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_33b363a9-61f9-4568-9026-babbd59ea1e4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What does \(d=-2\) represent in this context?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>This represents 2 days before the first estimate was taken.</para><para>This represents the day before the first estimate was taken.</para><para>This represents the day the first estimate was taken.</para><para>This represents 2 days after the first estimate was taken.</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 2 days before the first estimate was taken.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="a3bf1633-9c98-468d-96b9-797888d0cabe" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the estimated number of mosquitoes that were in the new swamp 1 day before the estimate was taken?
      </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>500</para><para>250</para><para>1,000</para><para>125</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.
    </para><para>The correct answer is 250.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="ad3dba8a-cb99-4c43-896e-7877ea939f47" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Use the following passage to answer questions 4 – 6.</para><para>A desert pond is slowly drying up. The average volume of the pond is shown in the table. The first year it was
        measured, the average volume was determined to be 40,000 liters. Double click on mathematical
        expression/equation to enlarge.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
        <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(y\), years</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>\(v\), volume (liters)</emphasis></entry></row>
        <row>
            <entry>
              –4
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              –2
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              40,000
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              20,000
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5,000
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
      <para>Which equation represents the pond’s water loss?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y=40,000\cdot\left(\frac12\right)^v\)</para><para>\(v=40,000\cdot\left(\frac12\right)^y\)</para><para>\(v=20,000\cdot\left(\frac14\right)^y\)</para><para>\(v=\frac12\cdot\left(40,000\right)^y\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is
        \(v=40,000\cdot\left(\frac12\right)^y\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_1aa16586-e2a9-4f03-81ba-c6cefedf6bc6" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What does \(y=-2\) represent in this context?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>the time it took for the pond to shrink by a factor of 2</para><para>the first time the volume was measured</para><para>the time 2 years after the first time the volume was measured</para><para>the time 2 years before the first time the volume was measured</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.
    </para><para>The correct answer is the time 2 years before the first time the volume was measured.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_0523a23f-0076-4431-b856-a144c4d029a5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What was the average volume of the pond 4 years before the first time the volume was measured?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>320,000 liters</para><para>160,000 liters</para><para>80,000 liters</para><para>640,000 liters</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.
    </para><para>The correct answer is 640,000 liters.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="f289d931-83cb-4e3b-adad-e0ecce980124" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which of the following is equivalent to 6,350,000 in scientific notation?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(6.35\times 10^4\)</para><para>\(6.35\times 10^5\)</para><para>\(6.35\times 10^6\)</para><para>\(6.35\times 10^7\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.
    </para><para>The correct answer is \(6.35\times 10^6\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_9de6da24-490a-47d4-a381-5749a1a2ba48" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which of the following is equivalent to 0.00032 in scientific notation?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(3.2\times 10^{-3}\)</para><para>\(3.2\times 10^{-4}\)</para><para>\(3.2\times 10^{-5}\)</para><para>\(3.2\times 10^{-6}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.
    </para><para>The correct answer is \(3.2\times 10^{-4}\).
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_643511df-673b-4103-a6a5-761446059723" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which of the following is equivalent to \(7.24\times 10^3\) in decimal form?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>7,240</para><para>724</para><para>72,400</para><para>724,000</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 7,240.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_31765884-975f-46fe-b3d1-76599c96e5d4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which of the following is equivalent to \(5.47\times 10^{-5}\) in decimal form?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>0.00547</para><para>0.0000547</para><para>0.00000547</para><para>0.000547</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 0.0000547.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="a543be8b-3931-41cd-87a0-e0cb9643cf50" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which of the following correctly orders these values from greatest to least?
          
          <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
            <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
                <entry><emphasis>Value R</emphasis></entry><entry>
                  0.00161
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis>Value S</emphasis></entry><entry>
                  \(6.35\times 10^{-3}\)
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis>Value T</emphasis></entry><entry>
                  0.000541
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis>Value U</emphasis></entry><entry>
                  \(7.23\times 10^{-4}\)
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody></tgroup></table>
      </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>Value S, Value R, Value T, Value U</para><para>Value R, Value S, Value T, Value U</para><para>Value S, Value R, Value U, Value T</para><para>Value R, Value S, Value U, Value T</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.5.
    </para><para>The correct answer is Value S, Value R, Value U, Value T.
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content></document>